  "authoringNote": "The final encounter states practitioner identifier SYN-PRAC-0001 and the final order states SYN-PRAC-0002, so the pair holds R04.practitioner_identifier_differs, a conflict for the administrative reviewer (SPEC R04 \"same treating practitioner\" and F04). Both documents state the same practitioner name, but C03 compares sameness by identifier only and names are not an R04 evidence field, so the equal names neither establish identity nor remove the conflict. R04 cites the status, date and practitioner identifier of both documents (six); the dates are in sequence and within the C01 bound 2027-02-20, so no chronology condition holds. A conflict on facts names no parent document (C07). R03 passes: the order states its own treating practitioner name and identifier and a signer name equal to its own practitioner name, with every other element (nine citations). The receipt follows the order date span (C06), so R05 passes. R01, R02, R07, R08 and R09 pass, R06 is qualified clinical review with five clinical citations and no administrative effect, and R10 is not applicable. The state is needs_human_review.",
